# Frequently asked questions

{% details title="Are deleted files removed immediately?" %}
No. Deleted files stay in the trash for 30 days and can be restored from the web console or with `nimbus restore`.
{% /details %}

{% details title="Can I pause syncing?" %}
Yes – from the icon in the notification area (the menu bar on macOS) or with {% kbd keys="Ctrl+Shift+P" /%}. Transfers already in progress are completed cleanly.
{% /details %}

{% details title="Which files are excluded?" %}
By default, temporary files such as `~$*.docx`, `.DS_Store` and `Thumbs.db`. You can add your own patterns with the `exclude` option.
{% /details %}

## Glossary {% #glossary %}

- [x] **Block** – fixed-size chunk of a file (4 MiB)
- [x] **Conflicted copy** – copy of a file that was edited in two places at the same time
- [x] **Version vector** – per-device counter used to detect conflicts
- [ ] **Selective sync** – planned for version 2.5

